# 2. The most important electrical diagrams to memorize

If I were preparing for a technical support job, I would make these diagrams my core reference library. They will help you understand most basic electrical and electronic systems.

## Diagram 1: Ohm's Law

EssentialWhat are the Limitations of Ohm's Law?

[shiksha.com](<https://www.shiksha.com/preparation/physics-current-electricity-limitations-of-ohms-law-5858-tp?utm_source=chatgpt.com>)

The most important electrical formula:

$$
V=I\times R
$$

Where:

- V = Voltage
- I = Current
- R = Resistance

The other two formulas:

$$
I=\frac{V}{R}
$$

$$
R=\frac{V}{I}
$$

Example: A 12-volt circuit has a 6-ohm resistance.

$$
I=\frac{12}{6}=2A
$$

You should be able to calculate these values without a calculator for simple numbers.

