# 4. Six types of diagrams you should become comfortable reading

The diagrams above show individual circuits and systems. For professional technical support, you also need to understand these six diagram formats.

| Diagram type | What it tells you |
| --- | --- |
| Electrical schematic | How components connect electrically |
| Wiring diagram | Physical wire connections and connectors |
| Block diagram | How the major sections of a device interact |
| Ladder diagram | How electrical control circuits operate |
| PCB layout | Where components are physically located on a circuit board |
| Pinout diagram | What each pin on a connector does |

Two additional useful formats:

- Timing diagrams: Show how digital signals change over time.
- Exploded-view diagrams: Show how mechanical and electrical parts fit together.

